+http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_1200262	sustentaculum tali of calcaneus	A zone of bone organ forming a horizontal, shelf-like medial projection of the calcaneus that supports the head and neck of the talus. Its superior surface bears the middle talar articular facet, its inferior surface is grooved for the tendon of the flexor hallucis longus, and it provides attachment for the plantar calcaneonavicular and medial talocalcaneal ligaments.	UBERON:0005913	UBERON:0001450	https://fipat.library.dal.ca/ta2/|ISBN:9780323393225|Wikipedia:Calcaneus	http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/uberon/core#added_by_HRA	2026-03-19T00:00:00Z	https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7073-9172	http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_9606
